a9y18qlte: Chlorophyll: framebuffer fetch before a6xx, as a texelFetch of the attachment

freedreno advertises fbfetch only on a6xx: ir3 compiles a [[color(n)]] read into a read of a texture
slot that only fd6 fills with the render target (patch_fb_read_sysmem in fd6_gmem.cc). On the A512
nothing is bound there and every fetch read zero. CoreAnimation's luma_boost_lph is a full-screen pass
that rewrites the frame from what it fetches, so every frame of backboardd's came out (0,0,0,0)
(214 of 214 traced frames with it; frames without it had content; the kernel showed the GPU writing
the very pages the panel copies). The rounded-corner clips fetch too.

Before a6xx each fetch (load_output with fb_fetch_output, after nir_lower_io) becomes a texelFetch at
the fragment's pixel from texture slot 15 - n, and rwa_render_draw binds colour attachment n there
(bind_stage). Such draws already render in sysmem behind a texture barrier, so the texture path reads
what the draws before them wrote.

Assisted-by: LLM

